cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formalization, please cite it as below."
title: "hoermander-rothschild-stein: a Lean 4 formalization of Hörmander's hypoellipticity theorem and the Rothschild–Stein theory"
abstract: >-
  A machine-checked Lean 4 / mathlib formalization of the regularity theory of
  Hörmander operators: Hörmander's hypoellipticity theorem; the
  Rothschild–Stein theory (lifting and approximation by homogeneous groups,
  the homogeneous fundamental solution, singular-integral estimates on
  homogeneous groups, and the interior Sobolev and Hölder estimates for sums
  of squares of vector fields, with and without drift); the formal
  Baker–Campbell–Hausdorff theorem; and Chow–Rashevskii connectivity and the
  Nagel–Stein–Wainger ball-box, volume and doubling theorems. On Carnot
  groups it constructs the heat kernel of the sub-Laplacian with two-sided
  Gaussian bounds, and proves the scale-invariant Poincaré inequality and the
  parabolic and elliptic Harnack inequalities and Hölder continuity for
  divergence-form operators with measurable, symmetric, uniformly elliptic coefficients.
  The development contains no sorry and no custom axiom.
type: software
